@page "/troubleshooting"

<PageTitle>Troubleshooting · Vela UI</PageTitle>

<div class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-10">
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <h1 class="text-title text-fg">Troubleshooting</h1>
        <p class="text-body text-fg-muted">Common problems when setting up Vela UI, and what fixes them.</p>
    </header>

    <DocSection Title="Restore can't find Vela.UI.Primitives" Id="package">
        <p>
            Components built on a primitive, such as Label, Checkbox, and Dialog, add a reference to the
            <code>Vela.UI.Primitives</code> package, which isn't on NuGet yet. Restore then fails with
            <code>NU1101</code>. Build the package from your clone and add a local source:
        </p>
        <CodeBlock Code="@Pack" />
        <CodeBlock Code="@NuGetConfig" />
        <p>
            Or replace the <code>PackageReference</code> that <code>vela add</code> added with a
            <code>ProjectReference</code> to <code>src/Primitives/Vela.UI.Primitives.csproj</code> in your clone.
        </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection Title="Components have no styles" Id="styles">
        <ul>
            <li>Check that the Tailwind watcher is running and writing the file your <code>App.razor</code> links.</li>
            <li>
                Tailwind has to read the component source, not the rendered HTML. The
                <code>@@source</code> line in <code>Styles/app.css</code> must cover your components folder,
                <code>.razor</code> and <code>.cs</code> files both. <code>vela init</code> writes it; update it
                if you move the folder.
            </li>
            <li>
                Tailwind doesn't move font files, so <code>fonts/</code> must sit next to the compiled CSS
                (<code>wwwroot/fonts/</code> by default).
            </li>
        </ul>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection Title="vela add stops with exit code 3" Id="conflicts">
        <p>
            A file it would write already exists with different content, usually because you changed it.
            Nothing was written; the message lists the files. To take the new version anyway, run it
            again with <code>--overwrite</code>. Your files are copied to <code>.vela/backups/</code> first.
        </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection Title="vela can't find your project" Id="project">
        <p>
            Run it in the folder that holds exactly one Blazor <code>.csproj</code> targeting .NET 10 or
            later, or pass that folder with <code>--cwd</code>. The message says which of these it
            couldn't confirm.
        </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection Title="Clicks, toggles, or a dialog do nothing" Id="render-mode">
        <p>
            The page is rendered statically, so nothing runs in the browser after it loads. Give the page
            or the component an interactive render mode, for example
            <code>@@rendermode InteractiveServer</code>. Each component's page lists what needs one.
        </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection Title="WebAssembly or Auto: components aren't found or don't respond" Id="client">
        <p>
            Interactive WebAssembly components run from the <code>.Client</code> project, so the components
            have to be installed there. Run <code>vela init</code> and <code>vela add</code> with
            <code>--cwd MyApp.Client</code>.
        </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection Title="A static form posts, but the values don't come back" Id="static-forms">
        <p>
            In a statically rendered <code>EditForm</code>, each field's posted name comes from its
            <code>@@bind-Value</code> expression. Bind to the property marked
            <code>[SupplyParameterFromForm]</code> itself, such as <code>@@bind-Value="Model!.Email"</code>,
            not to a copy of it. The <a href="static-form">static form</a> example shows the pattern.
        </p>
    </DocSection>
</div>

@code {
    private const string Pack =
        "dotnet pack path/to/vela-ui/src/Primitives -o ./packages";

    private const string NuGetConfig =
        """
        <configuration>
          <packageSources>
            <add key="local" value="./packages" />
            <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" />
          </packageSources>
        </configuration>
        """;
}
